WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.130
Two parallel plates face
each other in a vacuum,

2
00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.480
with 400 volts across them.

3
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.860
Send an electron between the plates.

4
00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:09.810
Then send a proton.

5
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.410
Their charges are equal and opposite.

6
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:16.800
So the forces on them are equal
in size, and point opposite ways.

7
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:22.500
Each force is tiny: 3.2 times
10 to the minus 15 newtons.

8
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:25.000
And gravity is far weaker still.

9
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.720
Fire both in parallel to the plates.

10
00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:30.640
Which one swerves more, and by how much?

11
00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:35.210
In this mission, you'll find the force
on any charge in a uniform field.

12
00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:40.230
Then you'll calculate how quickly an
electron gathers speed between two plates.

13
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.440
Your mission: predict which
particle swerves more,

14
00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:45.240
and estimate by how much.
